    "title": "South Side Residents Voice Gentrification Concerns Ahead of Obama Presidential Center Opening - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shelby Hawkins ,\n11 hours ago As the Obama Presidential Center prepares to open in Jackson Park this week, local activists continue to voice concerns about the potential displacement of longtime residents. Despite years of organizing and city ordinances being put in place, rising housing costs and investor activity continue to threaten gentrification in neighborhoods surrounding the center. Read full article",
